/**
	@help {
		Regenerate the A-map foundation math/mizar/miz_set.ru from the set.mm library.

		  cd ~/dev/math/set && russellj no-server=1 mem=12g translate/mizar/regen_foundation

		MUST be run from math/set/ — setmm2miz resolves `set_root` via the process CWD
		(not import-roots), so it must start where set_root.mm lives.

		Loads the set.mm Russell library (set_root), translates the kept fragment WITHOUT
		collapsing class→set (collapse=0 = native wff/setvar/class): the FOL calculus +
		the ZF "start with Extensionality" class layer (cun/cin/cdif/c0/csn + elun/eldif/
		ssel/sstr2/… — the lemmas the A-map needs), verifies, and writes math/mizar/
		miz_set.ru (~5133 assertions).

		NOTES (traps this handles): setmm2miz does NOT write a file — it loads the
		foundation into state, and the generated source's path is `<out-dir>/miz_set.ru`,
		so out-dir must be math/mizar and the write-ru below is what actually writes it
		(landing in math/mizar, NOT math/set which would pollute the set.mm library). The
		`keep` value must be UNQUOTED (the .rus arg layer keeps literal quotes → the
		fragment filter matches nothing → 0 assertions). `math` is provided automatically
		by bin/russellj from $RUSSELL_MATH.
	}
	@category translate
	@arg math { math root (auto from $RUSSELL_MATH; holds set/ and mizar/) }
*/

out := (math + "/mizar");

// out-dir sets the generated source's path to math/mizar/miz_set.ru, so write-ru lands there.
setmm2miz module=set_root keep=CLASSICAL_FIRST-ORDER_LOGIC_WITH_EQUALITY,ZF_(ZERMELO-FRAENKEL)_SET_THEORY/ZF_Set_Theory_-_start_with_the_Axiom_of_Extensionality,ZF_(ZERMELO-FRAENKEL)_SET_THEORY/ZF_Set_Theory_-_add_the_Axiom_of_Replacement,ZF_(ZERMELO-FRAENKEL)_SET_THEORY/ZF_Set_Theory_-_add_the_Axiom_of_Power_Sets,ZF_(ZERMELO-FRAENKEL)_SET_THEORY/ZF_Set_Theory_-_add_the_Axiom_of_Union collapse=0 out=miz_set out-dir=$out format=file;
verify;
	print ("regen verify: " + verify.success);
write-ru target=miz_set;
	print ("regen written: " + out + "/miz_set.ru");
